[4] Mazak INTEGREX i-400S Specs & Review (Discontinued Model)
URL: https://machinetoolindex.com/machines/mazak-integrex-i-400s
The Mazak INTEGREX i-400S is a twin-spindle multi-tasking machine with a B-axis milling head, listed with a maximum machining diameter of 658 mm (25.9 in) and a maximum machining length of 1,519 mm (59.8 in). Mazak no longer lists this model, so the figures here are the listed ones and should be confirmed against the build sheet of any machine on offer.

The listed main spindle runs to 3,300 rpm with 30 kW (40 hp), carries a 10 in chuck on an A2-8 nose and passes 102 mm (4.0 in) bar. The sub spindle is listed at 4,000 rpm and 22 kW (30 hp) with an 8 in chuck. It travels 1,562 mm on W, which is nearly the whole machining length, so it can pick a part off the main chuck or support a long shaft at its far end. C-axis rotation is 360° continuous on both spindles. The table does not say whether the power figures are continuous or short-time ratings.

Milling is done with a Capto C6 spindle listed at 12,000 rpm and 22 kW (30 hp), with 20,000 rpm as an option, on a B axis that swings 240° (-30° to +210°). The magazine holds 36 tools, with 72 or 110 optional. X travel is 615 mm (24.2 in) and Z travel 1,585 mm (62.4 in). Rapids are 50 m/min (1,969 ipm) on X and Z and 40 m/min (1,575 ipm) on Y, and the listed weight is 16,200 kg (35,714 lb).
