======================================================================
10. VARIABLE CASH FLOW MANAGEMENT STRATEGY
======================================================================

AS A FREELANCER WITH IRREGULAR INCOME:

Monthly Income Pattern (illustrative):
  Good months:  $10,000-$12,000 (3-4 months/year)
  Average:      $7,000-$8,000  (5-6 months/year)  
  Lean months:  $3,000-$5,000  (2-3 months/year)

STRATEGY: "Pay Yourself First + Buffer"
  1. Maintain a separate BUSINESS BUFFER account ($3,000-$5,000)
     to smooth income volatility before it hits personal accounts
  2. Set fixed monthly transfers on the 1st of each month:
     - Emergency fund replenishment (if needed)
     - RRSP: $1,425/month (= $17,100/yr)
     - TFSA: $583/month (= $7,000/yr)
     - RESP: $833/month (= $10,000/yr split $417/child)
  3. In HIGH-INCOME months: contribute extra to RESP catch-up
  4. In LOW months: draw from business buffer, skip discretionary saving
  5. Use RRSP contribution room carry-forward to "lump" in good years

RRSP SEASONALITY ADVANTAGE:
  Since RRSP room carries forward, you can:
  - Make smaller regular contributions ($1,000-$1,425/mo)
  - Make a large lump-sum before the March 1 deadline
  - Claim deduction in the highest-income year
