- DIY / part only: often about $35–$120+ for many mainstream replacement batteries, although premium, rare, high-capacity, or genuine parts can cost more.
- Independent repair shop: commonly the battery cost plus diagnosis and installation labor. A straightforward internal-battery job may still fit roughly in the $80–$200+ total range, while difficult ultrabooks can cost more.
- Manufacturer or authorized service: often $100–$300+, but exact pricing is highly model- and country-specific. Premium laptops, batteries bonded into larger assemblies, shipping, or additional damage can push the final bill higher.
...
Two laptops that cost the same when new can have very different repair costs. Battery capacity and shape affect the part price; a compact business laptop may use a smaller pack than a gaming notebook or workstation. Serviceability matters too: an older removable pack may take seconds to swap, while a thin modern laptop can require bottom-cover removal, delicate cable work, adhesive removal, or replacement of a larger assembly.

Part source also changes the bill. Genuine manufacturer batteries generally cost more than compatible packs, while third-party quality varies widely. Labor, taxes, import duties, hazardous-goods shipping rules, and regional availability can move the total again. That is why the only reliable quote is a model-specific one.
