The Greenhouse and Energy Minimum Standards (GEMS) Regulator supports the delivery of appliance and equipment energy efficiency policies under the Department of Climate Change, Energy, the Environment and Water (the department).

We achieve this by regulating products that must meet specified minimum energy performance standards and labelling requirements to be supplied in Australia.
...
The GEMS Regulator is responsible for administering the Greenhouse and Energy Minimum Standards Act 2012 (the Act) and supporting legislation in Australia.

The GEMS Regulator was established on 1 October 2012 to align state and territory energy-efficiency legislation for appliances and equipment.
