(2) Without limiting subsection (1), a person is taken to emit an unreasonable noise from residential premises if the person uses a prescribed item, except in a case of emergency—

(a) at any time prescribed as a prohibited time; and

(b) if noise emitted by that item can be heard in a habitable room in residential premises other than premises in which the item is being used, whether or not a window or door in that room is open.

