We introduce a new fault-tolerance scheme that is well-suited to state-of-the-art quantum computers. The scheme comprises a $16$-qubit “tesseract” code, sketched in Fig. 1, and methods for error correction and encoded computation. It is qubit efficient, with just a four-to-one overhead in qubit count, and also offers expeditious error correction (single shot, with only two extra qubits) and enough protection to reduce error rates substantially. The code is distance four, so three physical faults have to occur to cause a logical error.
