# Evert Jafet Calderon
...
Evert Jafet Calderon is a senior writer and spokesperson at Mesa Group Consulting. The son of Salvadoran immigrants and a first-generation American raised in Bakersfield, he has spent years across banking, financial consulting, and credit education, and now turns that experience into clear, honest financial guidance for the families Mesa serves in English and Spanish.

[5] About Mesa Group Consulting | Our Story, Mission & Team
URL: https://www.mesagroupconsulting.com/about
#### Evert Jafet Calderon
...
Evert was born in Los Angeles and raised in Bakersfield from the age of eight, the son of Salvadoran immigrants who came to this country chasing something better. Growing up as a first generation American meant he was often the one translating, not just language but life. Finances fascinated him early because he noticed a pattern. The families that got ahead understood money. The ones that struggled, including his own, never got the chance to learn. He joined a local credit union program in high school and never looked back, building a career that moved through banking, digital marketing, research and development, sales, and financial consulting before everything clicked into place at Mesa. He is, as he puts it, a true byproduct of the Mesa product. He has lived the journey firsthand and that is exactly why he understands it so deeply. Today his days are spent making sure operations run the way they should, working closely with lenders and realtors to prepare clients for homeownership, and constantly building the systems and platforms that make Mesa better for the people who need it. The client moments that stay with him are the ones where someone believed their life was over because of a three digit number. He has watched those same people open businesses, get keys to their first home, and finally buy the car they always wanted. He shows up every day because when he looks at his clients he sees his parents. The immigrant family with no support, no guidance, and no one who could speak their language and help them navigate a new life. Mesa is the answer he wishes they had always had.
