State-owned Housing and Urban Development Corporation Ltd (HUDCO) on Tuesday, December 9, said its Bond Allotment Committee is scheduled to meet on December 12 to approve the issue and allotment of unsecured, taxable, redeemable, non-convertible and non-cumulative debentures of face value ₹1,00,000 each, aggregating up to ₹2,500 crore on a private placement basis.

The proposal follows the approval granted by the board of directors on April 4, 2025, to raise funds up to ₹65,000 crore through the issue of bonds and debentures during FY2025-26. The proposed Series-E 2025 NCDs will have a tenure of seven years, with the redemption date fixed as December 12, 2032.

The debentures are unsecured in nature and constitute senior debt. The mode of issue will be private placement through the online bidding process on the BSE EBP platform. The issue size comprises a base size of ₹500 crore with a green shoe option to retain oversubscription of up to ₹2,000 crore, taking the total issue size to ₹2,500 crore.

The proposed NCDs carry a fixed coupon rate of 1% payable annually. The first interest payment date is December 12, 2026, with subsequent payments due annually up to maturity. The allotment is proposed to be made with a deemed date of allotment of December 12. The issue and bid opening and closing date are December 10 with the pay-in date being December 12. The proposed debentures will be issued at par at ₹1,00,000 per debenture.

