About this NCD
REC Limited has launched a Non-Convertible Debenture (NCD) issue at a coupon rate of 8.55% with a CRISIL AAA/Stable credit rating. The issue opens on 09 Dec 2025 and closes on23 Dec 2025. NCDs are fixed-income debt instruments that cannot be converted into equity shares — they offer regular interest payments and return of principal at maturity. Suitable for income-seeking investors looking for higher yields than bank fixed deposits while accepting the credit risk of the issuer.
Frequently Asked Questions
What is the REC Limited NCD coupon rate?
The coupon rate is 8.55% per annum.
What is the credit rating?
The NCD carries a CRISIL AAA/Stable rating, indicating the issuer's credit quality.
When does the issue open and close?
The subscription window opens on 09 Dec 2025 and closes on 23 Dec 2025, subject to early closure if fully subscribed.
What is the difference between an NCD and an IPO?
An IPO offers equity shares (ownership). An NCD is a debt instrument — investors lend money to the company and receive fixed interest, with no equity participation.
Are NCD returns guaranteed?
NCDs offer contractual interest payments, but they are not guaranteed by the government. Returns depend on the issuer's ability to honour interest and principal obligations — credit rating gives a proxy for this risk.
