[10] Form 121 for Bond Investors: TDS-Free Interest in India - Equirize (2026-07-03T05:52:04.000Z)
URL: https://www.equirize.com/resources/blogs/form-121-bond-investors-tds-free-interest-guide
Form 121 is a self-declaration given to the payer before income is credited or paid. In listed bonds and NCDs, that income is usually coupon interest. If your declaration is valid and accepted, the payer may credit interest without TDS.

The catch is eligibility. You cannot file Form 121 just because you dislike TDS or want higher cash flow. You file it only when your estimated tax liability for the tax year is nil. For many retirees, low-income investors, or investors with deductions and rebates, this can reduce refund paperwork.
...
Form 121 is the declaration prescribed under Rule 211 of the Income-tax Rules, 2026 for receipt of specified income without deduction of tax under Section 393(6) of the Income-tax Act, 2025. The Income Tax Department's official Form 121 guidance lists "interest on securities" as one of the covered income categories, which is why bond investors need to understand it.
...
