Edelweiss NCD 2025: Features, Ratings & Smart Investor Checklist
Piyush Prajapati03 December, 2025
Invest NowGet Expert AdviceTerm Sheet
Introduction
Many investors will look towards Fixed Income Investments, or Non-Convertible Debenture (NCD), for stable returns when interest rates are low; and therefore many well-established financial institutions offer NCDs as an attractive option. Recently, Edelweiss Financial Service Ltd. has come out with a secured and redeemable NCD with excellent yields, which has gained the attention of many investors who are seeking regular income through dependable investments due to their high rating.
This blog will go over some important information that potential investors should know about Edelweiss NCD. We will discuss some of the important features, why an NCD from Edelweiss is important and how you as an investor can determine whether or not an investment in this NCD will work for you within your portfolio.
Key Features of Edelweiss NCD
| Feature | Details
| Issuer | Edelweiss Financial Services Ltd.
| Instrument Type | Secured, Redeemable, Listed, Non-Convertible Debentures (NCDs)
| Credit Rating | CRISIL A+/Stable By Crisil Ratings Limited
| Issue Opens | 5 December 2025
| Issue Closes | 18 December 2025
| Minimum Investment | Rs. 10,000
| Effective Yield | 10.10%
| Coupon Rate | 8.85%-10.10%
| Tenor | Multiple tenors: 24, 36, 60 and 120 months depending on the series selected.
| Face Value | Rs. 1000 per NCD
Why Investors Consider Edelweiss NCD
High Fixed Returns
With coupon rates of approximately 11%, these NCDs yield even higher interest than most other fixed income investments such as bank fixed deposits which makes them highly attractive for both conservative and moderate-risk investors.
Credit Quality & Security
These NCDs are also secured with an A+ rating which generally means that investors will receive their interest and principal in a timely manner compared to unsecured loans or bonds.
Flexible Investment Periods & Payouts
Multiple tenors (2 to 10 years) and payout modes (monthly/annual/cumulative) provide flexibility to align with investors’ cash-flow needs and investment horizon.
Liquidity via Listing
Since the NCDs are listed on stock exchanges (e.g. BSE), investors may have the option to exit before maturity by selling on the secondary market — offering some liquidity compared to traditional long-term fixed-income products.
Lock-In or Exit Strategy:
Adding these Notes to an investor’s portfolio that already contains stocks, mutual funds or other high-volatility assets would provide many benefits, including greater stability, consistent cash flow, and a more balanced overall portfolio assumption.
What to Check Before Investing
Credit Risk: An NCD rated "A+" is considered a good rating; however, the NCD does not carry zero risk—investors should review the creditworthiness of EFSL overall and review its financial statements before purchasing.
Interest Rate Risk: By committing to a long-term NCD of 120 months, investors may risk having their effective cash flow affected if new instruments become more attractive due to rising market interest rates. As such, the market value of the older NCD could decrease.
Liquidity: Although the NCDs are listed, liquidity in the secondary market for NCDs may not be easily available, and it may not be easy to sell prior to maturity, thus preventing an acceptable return on investment.
Taxability: Interest paid to an investor as a junior secondary debt NCD may be taxable depending upon the investor’s income bracket; therefore, like with regular funding investment vehicles, the investor is subject to taxation on their NCD.
Lock-In or Exit Strategy: Before making an investment, it is important that investors are aware of the redemption terms, schedule of interest payments, and options for exit.
Who Should Consider Edelweiss NCD
Investors seeking steady, fixed income and looking for better yield than bank FDs.
Conservative to moderate risk-minded investors who desire portfolio safety with a regular interest payment.
An investor with a medium to long-term investment horizon (2-10 years depending on the chosen series).
An investor who would like to invest in retiree or fixed-income markets and require consistent cash flow (monthly or annually).
Investors looking to diversify away from stocks, mutual funds, and/or real estate.
How to Apply for Edelweiss Financial Services Ltd. NCD Online?
Registration with the Edelweiss Financial Services Limited NCD is also entirely online and hassle-free. Here are the steps involved:
Visit the Application Page
Go to the official RR Finance NCD page Edelweiss Financial Services LIMITED NCD
Enter Your Basic Details
Fill in your name, mobile number, and PAN number carefully.
Verify and Confirm
Select the NCD Re-check your details before proceeding to payment.
Pay Securely via UPI Modes
Complete your investment using UPI or other available online payment modes.
Allotment and Confirmation
After allotment, you will receive the NCD units directly in your Demat account.
Conclusion
Edelweiss Financial Services Ltd. has created an innovative fixed income product that combines competitive yields, a strong credit rating, flexibility in terms and conditions and a high potential for return on investment due to frequent turnover from the marketplace. Investors who are interested in receiving both a steady stream of income as well as the ability to actively trade their fixed income investments may find this particular type of non-convertible debenture to be an ideal addition to their overall investment strategy.
