[2] BelAZ to ship $3m worth of haul trucks to Mongolia (2017-08-04T16:26:09.000Z)
URL: https://eng.belta.by/economics/view/belaz-to-ship-3m-worth-of-haul-trucks-to-mongolia-103863-2017/
BelAZ to ship $3m worth of haul trucks to Mongolia
...
MINSK, 4 August (BelTA) – The Belarusian automobile engineering company BelAZ plans to ship three haul trucks worth nearly $3 million for a Mongolian company before the end of the year, BelTA learned from First Deputy Director of the Marketing Center of BelAZ Vasily Shostak.

BelAZ was visited by a delegation of Molgolia's Erdenet Mining Corporation. The visit resulted in a signing of an agreement on cooperation in maintenance and further supplies. “The parties agreed on a strategic partnership which also covers some organizational issues regarding vehicle maintenance. The agreement was reached to supply the Mongolian company with three haul trucks with the payload capacity of 130 tonnes worth about $3 million by the end of the year,” Vasily Shostak said. 

Erdenet Mining Corporation is one of the biggest ore mining and ore processing factory in Asia. It is a long-time partner of the Belarusian manufacturer. The fleet of vehicles of the Mongolian company consists mainly of BelAZ haul trucks with the payload capacity of 30, 45, 55 and 130 tonnes and also special-purpose mining equipment. 

In H1 2017 BelAZ supplied vehicles to 24 countries. The export to Russia rose by 32.7%, to other CIS countries by 41.2%, to non-CIS countries by 63.6%. As for non-CIS markets the biggest deliveries were made to Zimbabwe, Morocco, Angola, Bosnia and Herzegovina.

[3] Mining | Erdenet Mining Corporation
URL: https://www.erdenetmc.mn/en/operations/mining
Ore body of the copper-molybdenum deposit in the “Erdenetiin-Ovoo” stretches to the west from the east, 25 km in the length and 1.5-3 km in the width and consists of 4 main parts. The length of pit in the primary mining is approx. 2500 m, the width is approx.1500 m, the lowest level is 1265 m and the depth has been reached up to 120 m. The top of the mount was 1606m from the sea level in the initial period of operation. The pit is planned to have the ledge height of 15 m, the sidewall of 370-420, bench of 30 m and the least stripping area of 50 m. The ore body of copper-molybdenum consists of the minerals including chalcosine (Cu2S), chalcopyrite (CuFeS2), turquoise, bornite (Cu5FeS4), brochantite (Cu4SO4(OH)6), azurite (Cu3(CO3)2(OH)2), molybdenite (MoS2), delafossite (CuFeO2), tenorite (CuO), sericite and other minerals. Today LIEBHERR-994B hydraulic excavators from Germany, chain excavators including ЭКГ-10 and ЭКГ-15 from Russia operate for the mining works and drilling machine СБШ-250 MHA-32 are used for drilling. Chain and wheeled bulldozers such as Liebherr PK-764, Komatsu D-275A, WD-500, Caterpillar 824G, wheeled loaders L-581, WA 800, WA 600 and, motograders GD-825, CAT 16G etc., from USA, Japan, and Germany are used for spoil heap, road construction and repair for technological haulage. A powerful maintenance centre is running to perform all kinds of repair of mining equipment. The open pit annually produces 15000 tons of water resistant emulsion explosives. Australian “Orika Exsel” has been used for blasting and since 2009, the blasting has been conducted using the remote control blasting devices and apparatus from “Rothenbuhler engineering”, USA.

