[6] The Next Generation of Productive Hauling Begins with Uptime | Cat | Caterpillar (2025-04-07T00:00:00.000Z)
URL: https://www.cat.com/en_US/blog/next-generation-hauling-begins-with-uptime.html
Cat® 785, 789 and 793 mining trucks are infused with more than 30 new and improved features and technologies that deliver the next generation of productive hauling. They help operators work more efficiently and consistently. They enable machine responsiveness and controllability and improve cycle times.
...
Production is a priority on every mine site. But if machines are down, productivity isn’t possible. For its next generation of Cat 785, 789 and 793 mining trucks, Caterpillar has reduced key contributors to downtime with features such as:

- A new modular HVAC (heating, ventilation and air conditioning) system, which improves reliability and consolidates components so the entire system can be removed and replaced quickly.
- A modular radiator that reduces engine removal and installation time and enables rebuilds to be completed off the truck for reduced downtime.
- Remote Troubleshooting capabilities that reduce downtime ... performance by providing ... schedule updates when it’s most convenient to the operation
...
In addition, these trucks are designed to reduce the time spent on regular maintenance procedures. Improvements in serviceability and reliability include:

- Extended-interval filters with ground-level access
- Fluid-level sight glasses
- Grouped service points
- New centralized service center option
- Extended coolant life (12,000 hours)
- Extended hydraulic and TC/transmission filter life (500 to 1,000 hours)
- Cleaner hydraulic and electrical routings
- 100% airless electric start option, which eliminates air system maintenance from the machine and improves uptime
- Ground-level filters with extended service intervals for faster, safer planned maintenance

