# Detect periodic vibrato intent instead of synthesizing vibrato from generic motion energy
...
Make vibrato feel like a gesture the performer actually makes, not an LFO that XPI starts whenever the controller happens to move.
...
`Sources/XPadController/PressureAndVibrato.swift` currently derives vibrato energy from:
- right-stick frame-to-frame X movement;
- absolute gyro magnitude;
- trigger micro-velocity.

`InstrumentPerformanceEngine` passes `hypot(gyroX, hypot(gyroY, gyroZ))`, so gyro direction/axis information is discarded before vibrato interpretation.

The engine then converts the maximum energy into vibrato depth and generates a synthetic sine oscillator at roughly the instrument profile's default vibrato rate.

This means a broad one-off tilt, controller repositioning or transient recoil can create **periodic pitch modulation even though the physical gesture was not periodic**.
...
Gesture-recognition work treats segmentation of intentional dynamic gestures from incidental continuous motion as a first-class problem. Vibrato-specific motion analysis has successfully used periodic temporal structure such as autocorrelation rather than motion magnitude alone.
...
