New $0 retention for customers using the Coalition Incident Response services during a claim provides immediate access to dedicated in-house team

SAN FRANCISCO — December 2, 2020 — Coalition, the leading provider of cyber insurance and security, is now offering a $0 retention as part of its policy for insureds that use Coalition's in-house Incident Response services. For small to midsize businesses facing a cyber claim, this policy enhancement provides immediate access to Coalition’s dedicated Incident Response team, with no out-of-pocket retention expense for security and forensics services. 

Coalition’s in-house Incident Response team includes cybersecurity experts with previous government experience within the NSA, CIA, and FBI, as well as leading incident response firms and corporate security teams. This team is available to Coalition policyholders at no cost and has the authority, expertise, and experience to provide immediate assistance. With an average response time of under five minutes, Coalition Incident Response drastically reduces the costs and potential time lag when responding to attacks.

