❑ This study examined the internal structure of the NEPSY-II across three age groups (5–6, 6–7, and 13–16 years). ❑ Due to ongoing uncertainty regarding the NEPSY-II’s theoretical model and limited structural validation, it remains unclear what its scores truly reflect. ❑ Since individual subtest scores should not be interpreted in isolation, identifying which tests cluster within the same domain is essential. ▪ This will clarify how the scores can be meaningfully interpreted and applied in clinical contexts. ❑ Exploratory Factor Analysis (EFA) and Psychometric Network Analysis (EGA, bootEGA) were used to examine the structure and interpretability of the NEPSY-II scores.
