Two things stack on top of Manychat's sticker price for anyone paying from India. First, the plan itself is contact-metered: you're charged for every 'active contact' who touches an automation in a month, so the price rises with engagement and a viral post is a billing event. Second, the currency: Manychat bills in USD, so your bank applies its exchange rate plus a foreign-transaction markup (commonly around 3%), and GST at 18% applies on top. A '$15/mo' plan is therefore closer to ₹1,600 all-in — and only for as long as you stay at 500 contacts.

