Second degree AV block is where some of the atrial beats from the SA node don’t get through to the AV node. There are various subtypes of second degree AV block:

- Mobitz Type 1 (Wenkebach): There is progressive delay in conduction between the SA node in the right atrium and the AV node. This delay lengthens until there is a dropped beat. This then resets and the pattern repeats itself.

This rhythm creates a regular pattern which is safe. For many people, it is common during sleep, but sometimes occurs while awake too. Most people don’t have symptoms so it doesn’t need any treatment. Monitoring is needed though but if you don’t have any changes, you may be discharged from GOSH.
