URL: https://docs.github.com/en/actions/concepts/workflows-and-actions/reusing-workflow-configurations
Rather than copying and pasting from one workflow to another, you can make workflows reusable. You and anyone with access to the reusable workflow can then call the reusable workflow from another workflow.

Reusable workflows also complement agentic workflows: an agentic workflow can call approved, deterministic reusable workflows rather than duplicating logic. For more information, see Creating GitHub Agentic Workflows.

Reusing workflows avoids duplication. This makes workflows easier to maintain and allows you to create new workflows more quickly by building on the work of others, just as you do with actions. Workflow reuse also promotes best practice by helping you to use workflows that are well designed, have already been tested, and have been proven to be effective. Your organization can build up a library of reusable workflows that can be centrally maintained.
